WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.186
The next weekend my friends and I climbed aboard a big luxury bus.

2
00:00:05.187 --> 00:00:08.599
We were headed for our mountain getaway with Mr. Chen.

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.870
Bunch came too, of course.

4
00:00:10.871 --> 00:00:13.829
But he had to travel in his dog cage.

5
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.105
We found seats on the bus.

6
00:00:16.106 --> 00:00:20.225
All around us, lots of people were talking and laughing.

7
00:00:20.226 --> 00:00:24.689
I guess we weren't the only ones excited about a mountain getaway!

8
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.291
Caswell was sitting next to Molly.

9
00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:31.183
He had his huge teddy bear backpack with him.

10
00:00:31.184 --> 00:00:34.521
"Are we there yet?" he asked her.

11
00:00:34.522 --> 00:00:37.344
"Caswell, the bus hasn't even left yet,"

12
00:00:37.345 --> 00:00:41.959
said Molly, laughing at her little brother.

13
00:00:41.961 --> 00:00:45.254
"So how could we be there already?"

14
00:00:45.255 --> 00:00:49.707
The bus finally pulled out of the station a few minutes later.

15
00:00:49.708 --> 00:00:53.676
I smiled to myself and patted my backpack.

16
00:00:53.677 --> 00:00:59.496
Besides my clothes, the backpack contained my secret invention.

17
00:00:59.497 --> 00:01:04.492
From inside his dog cage, Bunch kept sniffing the air.

18
00:01:04.493 --> 00:01:09.640
He could probably smell the hamster pellets I had used for my invention.

19
00:01:09.641 --> 00:01:12.542
Bunch loves hamster pellets.

20
00:01:12.543 --> 00:01:14.984
He was even drooling!

21
00:01:14.985 --> 00:01:20.075
Mr. Chen had brought a big suitcase that held his magic tricks.

22
00:01:20.076 --> 00:01:25.977
When he wasn't working at the supermarket, Mr. Chen sometimes performed magic shows.

23
00:01:25.978 --> 00:01:30.708
Once I'd seen him make a frog leap out of his shirt sleeve.

24
00:01:30.709 --> 00:01:34.008
The audience had loved that trick.

25
00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:36.846
Molly had noticed the suitcase too.

26
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:41.765
"Mr. Chen, can we see your magic things?" she asked.

27
00:01:41.766 --> 00:01:45.248
"Sure," said Mr. Chen with a smile.

28
00:01:45.249 --> 00:01:47.476
"I'm working on some new tricks.

29
00:01:47.477 --> 00:01:51.126
I'm going to practice them at Shadow Lake Lodge."

30
00:01:51.127 --> 00:01:54.799
He took his suitcase down from the overhead rack.

31
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.069
He showed us some of the things inside:

32
00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:02.492
gold coins, playing cards, and a magic wand.

33
00:02:02.493 --> 00:02:06.417
"Are we there yet?" Caswell kept asking.

34
00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:09.274
Molly covered her face with her hands.

35
00:02:09.275 --> 00:02:12.157
But Josh smiled patiently.

36
00:02:12.158 --> 00:02:14.881
"Not yet, Caswell," he said.

37
00:02:14.882 --> 00:02:21.893
"But we're going into a cool tunnel now!" "This

38
00:02:21.894 --> 00:02:26.054
tunnel goes under a river," I added. Caswell

39
00:02:26.055 --> 00:02:30.468
peered nervously through the window. "I

40
00:02:30.469 --> 00:02:35.571
hope the river doesn't fall on our heads," he said. "Don't

41
00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:38.992
worry, Caswell," said Mr. Chen. "This

42
00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:40.639
tunnel is strong. It

43
00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.005
will keep the river out." When

44
00:02:43.006 --> 00:02:49.388
we came out of the tunnel, we were not in the city anymore. We

45
00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:52.048
were on a busy highway. In

46
00:02:52.049 --> 00:02:57.397
the distance I could see hills with colorful fall trees. An

47
00:02:57.398 --> 00:03:03.553
hour later the bus was climbing a steep mountain road. It

48
00:03:03.554 --> 00:03:11.556
led up to Shadow Lake Lodge. "Oh

49
00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:15.133
my gosh!" Jenny gasped. "

50
00:03:15.134 --> 00:03:19.144
This is where we're staying?" said Josh.

51
00:03:19.145 --> 00:03:26.106
"Caswell, guess what," Molly whispered. "We're finally here."

52
00:03:26.107 --> 00:03:30.361
I was staring at the building in amazement too.

53
00:03:30.362 --> 00:03:35.666
I decided that Shadow Lake Lodge wasn't really a hotel.

54
00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:39.708
It was a fairy-tale castle sitting on a mountain.

55
00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:43.157
Flags flew from its towers.

56
00:03:43.158 --> 00:03:46.202
Hills rippled below.

57
00:03:46.203 --> 00:03:51.267
A blue lake glittered in the sunlight.

58
00:03:51.268 --> 00:03:54.893
"I can't wait to see our room!" said Molly.

59
00:03:54.894 --> 00:03:58.962
"Maybe it will have gold curtains."

60
00:03:58.963 --> 00:04:02.697
"And diamond tables," said Jenny.

61
00:04:02.698 --> 00:04:07.799
Molly giggled. "We'll be like princesses!"

62
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:14.935
"Maybe we'll be invited to a fancy ball tonight," said Jenny.

63
00:04:14.936 --> 00:04:16.476
Josh gave me a look.

64
00:04:16.477 --> 00:04:19.838
The look meant, "Ugh! Girls."

65
00:04:19.839 --> 00:04:22.440
I knew just how he felt.

66
00:04:22.441 --> 00:04:26.702
I didn't care about gold curtains or diamond tables either.

67
00:04:26.703 --> 00:04:31.014
And I definitely didn't care about fancy balls.

68
00:04:31.015 --> 00:04:35.213
"I want to hike up to that lookout tower," I said.

69
00:04:35.214 --> 00:04:41.385
I pointed to a tall stone tower at the very top of the mountain.

70
00:04:41.386 --> 00:04:45.156
"Me too!" cried Josh.

71
00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:48.479
I had never climbed a mountain before.

72
00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:54.777
I patted my backpack again, really glad that I had brought along my latest invention.

73
00:04:54.778 --> 00:05:02.432
Looking up at the steep mountain, I had a feeling that we were going to need my invention.

